BT /F1 10 Tf 12 TL 56 760 Td (Brewbeacon) Tj T* () Tj T* (BREWBEACON: EXECUTIVE SUMMARY) Tj T* () Tj T* (Problem) Tj T* () Tj T* (Home brewing is a hobby built on patience, and its biggest frustration is inconsistency. A) Tj T* (brewer can follow the same recipe twice and get two very different beers. The usual causes are) Tj T* (invisible: fermentation temperature drifting overnight, yeast that stalls halfway, or a brewer) Tj T* (bottling before the beer has actually finished. Today most hobbyists check progress by pulling) Tj T* (a sample, floating a hydrometer in it, and reading a number by eye. Each sample risks) Tj T* (contamination and wastes beer, so most brewers check only once or twice and then guess.) Tj T* () Tj T* (We surveyed 212 home brewers through two regional brewing clubs and online hobbyist groups.) Tj T* (Sixty-eight percent said they had thrown out or been disappointed with at least one batch in) Tj T* (the past year because of a fermentation problem they did not catch in time. Fifty-four percent) Tj T* (said they do not measure gravity during fermentation at all. Brewers told us they wanted) Tj T* (reassurance and direction, not just data. That gap is the opportunity.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Solution) Tj T* () Tj T* (Brewbeacon is a compact sensor that clips onto the outside of a standard fermenter and measures) Tj T* (gravity and temperature continuously, sending readings to a mobile app every fifteen minutes.) Tj T* (Because it does not touch the beer, there is no contamination risk and no wasted sample.) Tj T* () Tj T* (The app is where the product becomes distinctive. A brewer selects a recipe, and Brewbeacon) Tj T* (builds an expected fermentation curve. As real readings arrive, the app compares them to that) Tj T* (curve and gives specific coaching: that the beer is running two degrees warm and should be) Tj T* (moved somewhere cooler, that fermentation looks finished and it is safe to bottle, or that a) Tj T* (stall suggests the yeast needs attention. Over time the app learns each brewer's setup and) Tj T* (recipes, so advice improves with every batch. The result is what brewers actually want: the) Tj T* (same good beer, again and again.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Market) Tj T* () Tj T* (There are an estimated 1.1 million active home brewers in the United States, based on industry) Tj T* (hobbyist surveys, and a larger group of casual and aspiring brewers who buy starter kits each) Tj T* (year. Brewers are an unusually committed customer. Our survey respondents reported spending an) Tj T* (average of 380 dollars per year on the hobby, and many already buy accessories and upgrades.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Our initial target is the roughly 300,000 brewers who brew at least eight batches a year and) Tj T* (already own a dedicated fermenter, since they feel the cost of failed batches most. If we reach) Tj T* (even five percent of that group, that is 15,000 customers. At our planned pricing, this) Tj T* (represents over 1.5 million dollars in hardware revenue and a recurring subscription base of) Tj T* (more than 500,000 dollars a year. The same sensor concept extends naturally to related) Tj T* (fermentation hobbies such as cider, mead, kombucha, and wine, which would widen the market) Tj T* (considerably.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Business Model) Tj T* () Tj T* (Brewbeacon earns money in two ways. First, we sell the sensor for 69 dollars, with a unit cost) Tj T* (of about 22 dollars at our planned first production volume, giving a gross margin of roughly 68) Tj T* (percent on hardware. Second, we offer an optional coaching subscription at 4 dollars a month or) Tj T* (36 dollars a year, which unlocks recipe-based curves, personalized advice, and batch history.) Tj T* (The sensor works with basic charting for free, so the subscription is a genuine upgrade rather) Tj T* (than a paywall.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Subscriptions matter because they turn a one-time purchase into recurring revenue with very low) Tj T* (marginal cost. In our current group of users, 24 of the 31 paying customers have chosen the) Tj T* (subscription, a conversion rate of about 77 percent among buyers. We also plan modest affiliate) Tj ET
endstream
